import research from '../platform-research.json';
const {base}=Astro.props;
---
<section class="report-closing campaign-actions" id="conclusion" aria-labelledby="conclusion-title"><div class="closing-inner">
<h2 id="conclusion-title">What to change next</h2>
<p class="campaign-intro">Make resource mobilization the organizing objective: reach relevant donors and delivery partners, demonstrate what UNDP can help them do, and give that interest a clear next step.</p>
<div class="content-actions">
<article><h3>Increase direct explanations to camera</h3><p>Test four additional short videos, each explaining one decision or trade-off in Riad’s own words. Record them alongside field visits and technical discussions.</p><p class="action-evidence">Nine identified to-camera videos received 114 median reactions, against 48 for other posts in the same months. A small sample to test further.</p></article>
<article><h3>Reduce invitation-led posts; increase event findings</h3><p>For each priority mission, publish the revealing exchange, finding or unresolved choice. Use an invitation when readers can participate; follow the event with something useful to people who were not there.</p><p class="action-evidence">Event reports: 74 median reactions and 4 comments. Invitations: 53 and 1, across the classified captions.</p></article>
<article><h3>Separate the photograph, chart and implication</h3><p>Test a document post with four clear pages: a field photograph, one sourced comparison, what it means, and the relevant opportunity to work with UNDP. Replace crowded composite visuals with one purpose per page.</p><p class="action-evidence">The visual review identified 11 chart, map or table posts. Carousel performance needs a separate test.</p></article>
<article><h3>Make the partner opportunity explicit</h3><p>Explain who could apply the method, use the tool or develop a project. Ask a specific professional question. Mention contributors when their experience is relevant, and develop useful replies into a focused follow-up.</p><p class="action-evidence">Only 13 of 243 classified captions were opportunity posts. LinkedIn’s <a href={research.sources.quality.url}>current guidance</a> favors substantive contributions and targets engagement bait.</p></article>
</div>
<section class="campaign-example" aria-labelledby="campaign-title">
<h3 id="campaign-title">One mission, one question, different treatments</h3>
<p>Before a priority mission, agree on the intended audience, the evidence to capture and the conversation to seek. For example, <strong>“Grids for development”</strong> could ask: <em>Which grid investments would allow local firms to connect, produce and grow?</em></p>
<div class="channel-treatments">
<article><h4>LinkedIn</h4><div><p>Develop Riad’s argument with a photograph from the work and one clear comparison. Ask utilities, investors or policymakers to assess the decision.</p><span>Outcome: informed professional discussion.</span></div></article>
<article><h4>Instagram</h4><div><p>Use an original short vertical clip and clean field photographs. Keep one line or key figure on a visual, with subtitles on video and context in the caption. Test Reels with non-followers where available.</p><span>Outcome: discovery and relevant profile visits.</span></div></article>
<article><h4>UNDP website</h4><div><p>Publish the evidence, methodology, country example and support available in a readable web page. Use a descriptive title, dated sources, related links and a clear contact route.</p><span>Outcome: search visibility and enquiries about the work.</span></div></article>
<article><h4>Internal email &amp; briefings</h4><div><p>Send a short, tailored note to relevant country and regional teams. Invite a selected audience to a JET methodology session or digital-tool demonstration when it addresses a defined need. Agree on an application and the next discussion.</p><span>Outcome: introductions, technical requests and partner opportunities.</span></div></article>
</div>
<p class="platform-reference"><a href={research.sources.metaTrials.url}>Instagram testing</a> · <a href={research.sources.googleAI.url}>Search and AI discovery</a> · <a href={base+'research/#channels'}>Channel evidence</a></p>
</section>
<section class="partner-outcomes" aria-labelledby="outcomes-title">
<h3 id="outcomes-title">Track the next conversation and what it leads to</h3>
<div><article><h4>Relevant discussion</h4><p>Technical questions, evidence requests and peer referrals from the intended professional audience.</p></article><article><h4>Qualified follow-up</h4><p>Briefing requests, meetings and agreed next steps, with a responsible colleague and campaign reference.</p></article><article><h4>Partner opportunity</h4><p>Requests for technical support, concepts developed and donor discussions. Record confirmed funding separately.</p></article></div>
<p class="platform-reference">Compare content at the same age, using reach where available. Review website and AI visibility with the web team through <a href={research.sources.googleMeasure.url}>Search Console</a> and <a href={research.sources.bingMeasure.url}>Bing Webmaster Tools</a>.</p>
</section>
</div></section>
